            <description><![CDATA[<h2>Jarvis 0.15.4</h2>

<p><b>Jarvis starts on macOS Sonoma again.</b> On macOS 14 the app quit before it
ever drew a window — macOS showed only "Jarvis can't be opened", with no reason.
Anyone still on Sonoma could install Jarvis and never see it run.</p>

<h3>What was wrong</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Two floating panels — the sync overlay and the "start a transcript?"
      meeting prompt — were built at launch, while the main window was still
      being constructed. On macOS 15 and later that is harmless. On macOS 14 it
      trips an assertion deep inside SwiftUI and the app stops instantly.</li>
  <li>Both panels are now created the first time they are actually shown, which
      is long after the window exists.</li>
</ul>

<p>Nothing else changed: same screens, same data, same sync. If you are on macOS
15 or later you were never affected and will notice no difference.</p>
]]></description>
